--- body ---
## Context
`erg init --help` treats `--help` as a directory argument, calls
`os.MkdirAll("--help/tickets/", 0755)`, and creates a directory on disk.
The same mis-handling affects any subcommand that accepts an optional DIR
arg: `check`, `ready`, `next-id`, `archive`, `migrate`, `init`.

The `main()` switch handles `-h`/`--help`/`help` only when they appear as
the *command* (position 1), not as a subcommand flag (position 2+).

## Actions
1. In `main()`, after splitting `cmd` / `rest`, check if `rest` contains
   `--help` or `-h` and call `printUsage()` + exit 0 before dispatching.
   One guard covers all subcommands uniformly.

## Test
```
erg init --help   # must print usage and exit 0, not create --help/ dir
erg check --help  # same
erg new --help    # same
```
Red: currently creates `--help/tickets/` on disk (or prints confusing error).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg init --help` prints usage and exits 0; no directory created
- [ ] Same for `erg check --help`, `erg ready --help`, `erg next-id --help`
- [ ] `make test` passes
